// Zero-argument readers of node 0's kind/a/b fields, wrapping k_of/a_of/
// b_of at the fixed index a fresh store's first node always gets. `then`
// only names zero-argument functions, so a case proving what push_kab (or
// anything that ends up building node 0) actually stored needs one of
// these rather than calling k_of/a_of/b_of directly. get/ has no room for
// a sibling file, so set.id was promoted into set/ to make room.

k0_of() {
  string s = k_of(0);
} return string s;
given kab_fixture ():("tok")
given boot_a given exprfix stdin "5;" ():("num")

a0_of() {
  int v = a_of(0);
} return int v;
given kab_fixture ():(5)
given boot_a given exprfix stdin "9;" ():(9)

b0_of() {
  int v = b_of(0);
} return int v;
given kab_fixture ():(7)
given boot_a given exprfix stdin "5;" ():(0)
